{
    "background_story": "Charli was a free-spirited poet who drew inspiration from the Norse god of poetry, Bragi. She spent her days wandering the rolling hills and forests, seeking the perfect words to capture the beauty of the world around her. Charli's love for Bragi's stories and poems led her to create her own mythology, weaving tales of love, loss, and the human condition. Her writing was infused with the same passion and creativity that Bragi was said to possess. As she traveled from town to town, sharing her verses with anyone who would listen, Charli became known as the modern-day Bragi, spreading joy and inspiration through her words. Her poetry was a testament to the power of art to bring people together and transcend time.",
